From: RNSBox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: sophgo: clock the EVB SLIP UARTs at 96 MHz

Set the camera PLL to 96 MHz at UART probe time; UART1/UART2 take it as
their baud clock (previous patch), which makes the modem 2 Mbaud exact.

The assignment lives on the uart2 node (not the clock controller) so it
runs after the clock framework is up; clk_cam0_200 stays on the crystal
for the console and disppll is not touched at all.

--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-duomodule01-evb.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-duomodule01-evb.dts
@@ -304,9 +304,6 @@
  * this mux in a state Linux can rely on, so pin parent and rate here.
  */
 &clk {
-	assigned-clocks = <&clk CLK_CAM0_200>;
-	assigned-clock-parents = <&clk CLK_DISPPLL>;
-	assigned-clock-rates = <96000000>;
 };
 
 /*
@@ -325,6 +322,11 @@
  * and the UART card in Settings shows it. UART1 is muxed by S31slip; the
  * other pads need a board-specific fmux setup before use. */
 &uart2 {
+	/* Programmed at probe: of_clk_init runs before the timers, and the
+	 * PLL lock poll never returns there. */
+	assigned-clocks = <&clk CLK_CAM0PLL>;
+	assigned-clock-parents = <&clk CLK_MIPIMPLL>;
+	assigned-clock-rates = <96000000>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&uart2_cfg>;
 	status = "okay";

